rial advantage of roughly 2 points (rook = 5, bishop = 3). Also, the rook on c1 is unprotected, so it’s a clean capture. This weakens white’s coordination and removes a key attacker from the board. Other moves like rook centralization or pawn capture are useful but less immediately impactful in gaining a decisive advantage.\n\n**Answer:** B: d2-c1'}
