er white king moves, bishop has no safe square and may be trapped if white brings rook or knight. It also doesn’t improve Black’s structure.  \nBetter is to improve king safety and activate rook. **R: h8-e8** centralizes rook, puts pressure on e-file, prepares possible doubling on e-file later, and gets rook off potentially vulnerable back rank (though no immediate threat). Also keeps options for king to move later. Alternatively, Kc8-b7 is safe but passive.  \n\nGiven Black’s pawn majority on queenside, activating rook and preparing to push pawns seems prudent. **R: h8-e8** is a solid, flexible move that improves Black’s position without creating weaknesses.\n\nAnswer: R: h8-e8'}
