-b6? would leave White king only a8 (no legal move, not in check → stalemate). So not Qb6.\n\nBest is to use queen to limit the king’s mobility while keeping check threats that force king toward corner without stalemating. King move toward white king is also good.\n\nReason:  \nI choose **Q: d6-d7** because it immediately attacks b7 (which would be mate if white king stays on a7/a8) and forces white king to a6. Then black’s king can move toward d5 or c5 next move, and queen will soon deliver mate with support. This keeps initiative and avoids stalemate.\n\nAnswer: Q: d6-d7'}
